                <pb facs="0566" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg516"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Document No. 4.—From Lisbon to Rio de
                        Janeiro.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-12"><hi rendition="#small-caps">March</hi> 12,
                        1894</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Command of corvette Mindello:</hi></p>
                <p>You should proceed there in harmony with the chargé d’affaires of Portugal, who
                    receives instruction from the Government. Chargé d’affaires has already
                    telegraphed to the Government about the asylum and mediation sought by Gama.
                    Chargé d’affaires will proceed according to instructions of Government, which he
                    will communicate to you for due performance. In the present state of affairs
                    there it is essential for each one to do his duty, laying aside all personal
                    feeling. I can not at this moment grant release to one who, like you, occupies a
                    post of importance and confidence.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Neves Ferreira</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
